! A magnetic insulator small enough to carry a sum over states: a chain of
! hydrogen trimers with unequal spacings (1.6, 1.8 and 2.0 bohr), the chains
! 7 bohr apart, held at one Bohr magneton a cell by fixed occupations. The up
! channel fills two bands and the down channel one, so the two channels are
! filled to different depths, which is what an nspin = 2 chi_0 has to get
! right and an unpolarized cell cannot test. The spacings are all different,
! so no band is degenerate with its neighbour at any k and neither cut splits
! a multiplet. The whole unshifted 1x1x8 grid with nosym and noinv, as the
! sum over states needs.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, nat = 3, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    nspin = 2
    occupations = 'fixed'
    tot_magnetization = 1
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.3
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.4
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
CELL_PARAMETERS bohr
 7.0 0.0 0.0
 0.0 7.0 0.0
 0.0 0.0 5.4
ATOMIC_POSITIONS bohr
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
 H 0.0 0.0 1.6
 H 0.0 0.0 3.4
K_POINTS (automatic)
 1 1 8 0 0 0
